    <outline text="Mashup: The Dog Smells like Roses - 99x via [MashupTown &lt;http://mashuptown.com/&gt;]"/>
    <outline text="Apple iTunes Your iTunes Affiliate Application Status">
      <outline text="Dear Adam Curry:&#10;&#10;We regret to inform you that iTunes has chosen not to accept your application for the iTunes Affiliate Program at this time.  This may be because:&#10;&#10;-- The content is unrelated to iTunes&#10;-- Your site is temporarily down or under construction ¿-please make sure to apply again after 2 weeks.&#10;-- A wrong or misspelled URL given in the application.  Please correct the problem and apply again.&#10;-- Your site is aesthetically unpleasing&#10;-- Your site promotes tobacco, alcoholic beverages or excessive drinking/drug use&#10;-- Your site contains extreme religious content&#10;-- Your site is international (with a majority of visitors based OUTSIDE the US. or written in a foreign language)&#10;&#10;If any of the above problematic criteria can be resolved, we look forward to your reapplication.&#10;&#10;If you plan to reapply in the next two weeks, you must do so at the following link because of restrictions by the LinkShare network.  Please reapply and we will gladly reconsider.&#10;&#10;alogin.linksynergy.com—sterm.shtml &lt;http://alogin.linksynergy.com/php-bin/affiliate/join/sterm.shtml?o_id=78941&gt;&#10;&#10;&#10;If you have any questions or concerns, please feel free to email us at itunesaffiliates@apple.com &lt;mailto:itunesaffiliates@apple.com&gt; or contact@linkshare.com. &lt;mailto:contact@linkshare.com.&gt;&#10;&#10;Thank you for your interest in the iTunes Affiliate Program.&#10;&#10;Best Regards,&#10;&#10;iTunes Affiliate Team&#10;www.itunes.com—affiliates &lt;http://www.itunes.com/affiliates&gt;"/>
    </outline>
    <outline text="Bar Stool Today!">
      <outline text="Tom Hickey"/>
    </outline>
    <outline text="Is mijn podcast ervaring uniek?">
      <outline text="Dag Adam,&#10;&#10;Ik download al sinds januari je podcast en vind je gebabbel leuk om naar te luisteren, vooral als er Nederlands gesproken wordt.&#10;&#10;Ik vraag mij af of er nog mensen zijn die hetzelfde ervaren als ze naar podcasts luisteren, spreek er eens over tijdens je podcast:&#10;&#10;I listen a lot to podcasts when I walk to the office and when I work out: running, riding my mountainbike and race-bike, bouldering, ...&#10;I've noticed that locations can trigger my memory about a particular podcast. It happened again today: I rode my mountainbike along a route I take frequently (west of Brussels) and at a certain road crossing I remembered a discussion about a new tablet PC on the Tablet PC Show I had listened to the previous time I rode past that location.&#10;It's a kind of reverse soundseeing: things I see trigger sounds I heard.&#10;&#10;Have you experienced this or have people mentioned this to you?&#10;&#10;Thanks for the show, en wanneer komt er nog een PPP?&#10;&#10;Didier Stevens,&#10;&#10;Brussel"/>
    </outline>
    <outline text="PSA: Katrina wichita"/>
    <outline text="Promo: Gaming Edge Weekly"/>
    <outline text="DS and GBA explained">
      <outline text="Michael Shotter 	&#10;&#10;Hello,&#10;&#10;    I'm sure plenty of other nerds will jump on this, but I figured&#10;I'd join the chorus.&#10;&#10;The DS is the &quot;Nintendo DS,&quot; Nintendo's latest handheld gaming&#10;device. The letters DS refer to the system's Dual Screens, which&#10;allow unique display and input options for games.&#10;&#10;The GBA is the GameBoy Advance, which was Nintendo's previous&#10;handheld system, still in wide use by gamers and backward compatible&#10;with original GameBoy games.&#10;&#10;For more information on current gaming platforms and operating&#10;systems, check out our State of the Game article on Gaming's Edge.&#10;&#10;www.gamingsedge.com—viewcontent.cfm &lt;http://www.gamingsedge.com/viewcontent.cfm&gt;?&#10;content=21&amp;content_type=Article&amp;department=1&#10;&#10;And yes, I'm going to bug you again about playing the promo for our&#10;&quot;Gaming's Edge Weekly Roundup&quot; podcast. Here's a direct link to the&#10;promo:&#10;&#10;www.gamingsedge.com—gewrpromo.mp3 &lt;http://www.gamingsedge.com/podcasts/gewrpromo.mp3&gt;&#10;&#10;and our podcasting info page:&#10;&#10;www.gamingsedge.com—info.html &lt;http://www.gamingsedge.com/podcasts/info.html&gt;&#10;&#10;Hope this is useful.&#10;&#10;Michael Shotter (a.k.a. VorTech)"/>
    </outline>
    <outline text="Katrina relief auctions going on right now">
      <outline text="Dear Mr. Curry, (I know you're not THAT old) :)&#10;I was listening to your podcast this morning when you spoke of Hurricane Katrina and asking for us to let you know of any ways that people can help the victims of this devastation. My new podcast Boutique Café is almost ready to launch and we'll be doing a show late this week about hurricane Katrina and how people can help and get involved. Our Boutique Selling community is vast and a big hearted group. Many of our fellow designers that we know have lost their homes and all their possessions. Fellow designers have joined together to give from our hearts. Please go to eBay and search &quot;Boutique Angels&quot;, these talented designers are donating 100% of the proceeds through the verifiable eBay charity association of Mission Fish to MERCY CORPS - Hurricane Katrina fund. These sellers are giving of their talents, time, and materials to making some beautiful boutique items so please ask your listeners to check the auctions out and bid on some gorgeous one of a kind items to support Mercy Corps and those that need so much right now.&#10;Sincerely,&#10;Daria Muirhead&#10;Boutique Café&#10;www.boutiquecafe.com &lt;http://www.boutiquecafe.com/&gt;"/>
    </outline>
    <outline text="Biodiesel - Crap in your Tank">
      <outline text="I love your biodiesel idea about being able to crap in your tank. I think we need to talk to Roto-rooter about some joint development of this technology. I mean, if they're pumping the stuff out of my septic tank already, why can't they pump it back into my gas tank.&#10;&#10;Of course, if the cooking oil biodiesel smells like french fries...&#10;_____________________________&#10;Bill Lefler"/>
    </outline>
    <outline text="Podsafe Music Network &lt;http://music.podshow.com/&gt; Podcaster Terms &lt;http://music.podshow.com/music/producerTerms.htm&gt;"/>
    <outline text="MTV VMA's">
      <outline text="James Martin 	&#10;&#10;actually I found out that Sean combs didn't give &quot;his&quot; watch to the guy in the audience well he did but after that during the commercial break a security guard came down and asked him to take the watch and they did give him a watch but it was a cheap knockoff of the actual watch. &#10;"/>
    </outline>
    <outline text="Biddies Live &quot;Famous&quot; [Site &lt;http://biddies4ever.com/&gt;]"/>
    <outline text="Kids complaining about parents">
      <outline text="Hi,&#10;I'm a 17 year old teen from Australia and just wanted to pipe in that not all parents are horrible! Since I'm a fourth child (catholics...) my parents have pretty much accepted I'm going to grow up and that I want my privacy. That respect helps make a good relationship between my parents. Just thought I would tell you that not all parents and teens have hate each other!"/>
    </outline>
    <outline text="PodSafe: Griddle - Preoccupied [Site &lt;http://griddle.cc/&gt;]">
      <outline text=" San Francisco's GRIDDLE just released its second album, Turning Violet, with a southwestern tour that took the boys across Texas. Members Kimo Ball, Xifer Fortier, Chris McGrew, and Kevin Seal enjoy volume, alcohol, melodies and confusion. Their songs are strange but catchy. More at Griddle."/>
    </outline>
